entry.summary:
Installing an npm package takes a few seconds.
npm install some-package
And that's exactly why it's so easy to overuse them. Need a date formatter? Install one. Need a UUID? Install one. Need to validate an email? Install one. Need to check if an array contains something? 😭 There's probably a package for that too. But every dependency you add becomes part of your project. So before running npm install, I started asking myself five questions. This is the first question. Sometimes the functionality you need is already available in JavaScript. For example, you don't need a package just to remove duplicates from an array: const unique = [...new Set(numbers)];
Or to check whether an array contains a value: numbers.includes(10);
The point isn't: "Never use packages." The point is: Don't…
